/*********************************************** JAVA **************************************************/

Optimal Solution - Kadane’s Algorithm to find the maximum sum subarray in linear time.
                  At every index, I decide whether to start a new subarray or extend the previous one, while keeping track of the global maximum.

class Solution {
    public int maxSubArray(int[] nums) {
        // maxSoFar stores the maximum subarray sum found so far
        int maxSoFar = nums[0];
        // currMax stores the maximum subarray sum ending at the current index
        int currMax = nums[0];
        // Traverse the array starting from index 1
        for (int i = 1; i < nums.length; i++) {
            // Either start a new subarray at nums[i]
            // OR extend the previous subarray
            currMax = Math.max(nums[i], nums[i] + currMax);
            // Update global maximum
            maxSoFar = Math.max(currMax, maxSoFar);
        }
        return maxSoFar;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(N).
Space Complexity :- O(1).
